  "proof": "For each scan assigned to query i, a fixed signed left sum and each of M unordered right-point pairs matches at most one Q_i. Its uniform nonidentity marginal gives probability at most 1/(r-1), even with correlated queries. Linearity bounds expected representations by S*h*M/(r-1); rank is no larger; Markov gives S >= ceil(0.95*K*(r-1)/(h*M)).",
